MATH 4.189.solution_overview:
A parametric linear Gleichung $k\,x = b$ is classified by its coefficient: $$k \neq 0 \implies \text{exactly one solution } x = \frac{b}{k}$$ $$
k = 0,\ b = 0 \implies \text{infinitely many solutions}
$$ $$k = 0,\ b \neq 0 \implies \text{no solution}$$ Hier verschwindet $k = a^{2} - 4 = (a-2)(a+2)$ genau für $a = 2$ und $a = -2$.
